 you that don't know  george rr martin wrote some of the  episodes for game of thrones he actually  wrote one episode for each of the first  four seasons of the show the very last  episode he wrote was the lion and the  rose the episode famously known for  joffrey's wedding now what's really  interesting about this episode is you  can go online and read an early version  of this script written by george rr  martin this early draft of the lion in  the rose differs wildly from what ended  up airing on hbo and what makes this  even more interesting are some of the  notes george r martin left for writers  david and dan  one of these notes actually reveals a  scene that will happen in the winds of  winter the author was hoping they would  show it on game of thrones in one of the  later seasons but they never did so as  of right now the scene still hasn't  happened in any format let me show you  what his note says it says a note for  future reference a season or two down  the line ramsay's pack of wolfhounds are  going to be sent against the stark  direwolves so we should build up the  dogs as much as possible in this in  subsequent episodes the reason why he  left this note here is because of the  opening scene in the episode the very  first scene in the last episode written  by george rr martin showed ramsay  sending his hounds after one of the  girls he was abusing in winterfell  she thinks she's pretty  let me put one through her face  you have to reward the hounds  they did all the hard work  but you made miranda feel jealous be  jealous of her  as you can see by the note george was  setting up the hounds for a much larger  scene down the road eventually he would  have all of them face off against the  stark direwolves now if i just look at  the scene on its surface level the  little boy inside of me thinks this  sounds awesome who doesn't want to see  ramsay's hounds fight against the stark  direwolves that would be amazing  especially in the show format because  yo